    <h2>Benefits of Sustainable Agriculture</h2>
    <ul class="agriculture-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Food Security:</strong> Ensures a stable and sufficient food
        supply for future generations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Soil Conservation:</strong> Reduces soil degradation and
        promotes soil fertility.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Water Conservation:</strong> Uses efficient irrigation
        techniques to minimize waste.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Biodiversity Preservation:</strong> Encourages crop rotation and
        organic farming to maintain ecological balance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Economic Growth:</strong> Provides employment and supports rural
        communities.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Modern Farming Techniques</h2>
    <p>
      With advancements in technology, agriculture has evolved to include
      precision farming, hydroponics, and organic farming. These methods help
      maximize yield while reducing environmental impact.
    </p>
